support for impacted stool, but lack of imaging weakly reduces its likelihood."}, {"t": 4, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the wife's recent cruise-related gastroenteritis and the patient's subacute symptoms support norovirus as the etiology despite the absence of fever or bloody diarrhea?", "summary": "Epidemiologic link to cruise weakly supports norovirus, but subacute timeline moderately reduces likelihood."}, {"t": 4, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the patient's anxiety history support a functional gastrointestinal disorder interpretation despite the systolic murmur and severe hypertensive crisis?", "summary": "Anxiety provides weak support for functional GI disorder, but cardiovascular instability moderately argues against it."}, {"t": 4, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of documented fecal impaction or specific imaging findings rule out adhesions-related mechanical obstruction despite the abdominal scar and chronic constipation?", "summary": "Lack of imaging moderately argues against adhesions-related obstruction despite clinical risk factors."}, {"t": 4, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the lack of documented fecal impaction or imaging findings argue against impacted stool as the primary cause given the patient's subacute symptoms?", "summary": "Absence of imaging moderately reduces impacted stool likelihood despite chronic constipation and distension."}, {"t": 4, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the subacute time course for symptoms argue against infectious gastroenteritis (e.g., norovirus) which typically presents acutely despite wife's similar symptoms?", "summary": "Subacute timeline moderately reduces norovirus likelihood despite epidemiologic risk from wife's symptoms."}], "differential_history": [{"top": [["B1", 0.366], ["B2", 0.209], ["B5", 0.189]]}, {"top": [["B1", 0.244], ["B2", 0.18], ["B5", 0.135]]}, {"top": [["B1", 0.248], ["B5", 0.165], ["B2", 0.146]]}], "deliberation": {